{
  "requirement": "Configure the domain’s project files with {cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_sources`. `Domain::project_sources` binds those files to the domain for Rust searches and agent inspection. Each hit identifies a node under {cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.sources.provider.attachment`**\n1. Project files configured with `with_sources` are attached to the domain's cache.\n2. `Domain::project_sources` binds those files to the domain, so searches and agent inspection use them. With no attached files there is nothing to bind.\n3. Each hit identifies a node under `requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`. That is a domain `NodeId` obtained through `Domain::source_node`.\n\n**Test mapping**\n- `configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions` (in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs`, `mod[tests]`) builds the domain with `ValidationCache::with_agent(config).with_sources(Sources::new(dir))`. It runs the configured agent twice against a local transport.\n  - The tool list includes `list_sources`, `outline_source`, `search_text`, `search_structure` and `finish_search`. That shows `project_sources()` returned `Some` and bound the sources to the agent.\n  - `list_sources` returns ids that are all integers, so they are domain node ids.\n  - `read_node` with an unknown id is rejected with \"invalid node ID\". `read_node` of a listed id returns the domain's snapshot text, not the disk contents.\n  - `search_text` hits carry nodes. The final dependencies list exact domain nodes (`TestNode` ids 8, 9 and 10) with fingerprints derived from the file contents. The test also asserts that `domain.source_node` was called with `OutlineId(\"visible/selected.txt\", \"\")`, and only for the visible, non-ignored file. This establishes that hits are mapped through the domain under `source_nodes`.\n- `domain_without_project_sources_leaves_source_tools_disabled` (in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs`) covers the negative case: a domain without attached sources returns `None` from `project_sources()`.\n- `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` is also marked. It adds only a negative check that a domain without sources still works. It is not the main evidence.\n\n**Residual consideration**\nNo test marked for this requirement calls `domain.project_sources()` directly and runs a Rust-API `search_text` or `search_structure` on the attached project. `SourceProject::search_text` and `search_structure` share `find_hits`. The agent's `search_text` dispatch uses that same `SourceProject` object returned by `project_sources()`. The Rust-API search behavior is also tested separately in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs`, for example `structural_tags_select_only_the_original_enclosing_item`. That test builds `ProjectSources` directly and is marked for `SourceProject`, not for this requirement. `Domain::project_sources` itself only clones the configured sources and the domain into a `SourceProject`, so I did not treat this as a gap.\n\nThe requirement is adequately tested, covering the attached case, the unattached case, and node identification of hits through the domain. There are no acknowledged gaps.",
  "references": "6c8ce8157893ac62f7994d2ab6e8b2ce8aea5bbb38571d10c5ffa8d4eb885fad",
